      "section": "Signal matrix",
      "order": 3,
      "alignment": "left",
      "vertical_alignment": "top",
      "body": "One row per ATAC-seq peak, one column per 50 bp offset from the summit, cell colour is the normalised signal. Rows are ordered by total signal and split into a panel per peak class, so the banding is the reading: promoters give a narrow bright stripe with faint nucleosome shoulders either side, enhancers a broad low mound, background peaks almost nothing. Columns are positions and are never reordered; past the row budget rows are averaged into bins rather than truncated, so the weak half never disappears.\n",
      "wf_tag": "python/advanced_viz_demo"
    },
